  "notes": "Combines the nuances of visiting and investigating. Often implies going somewhere with purpose — to discover, report on, or appreciate something. Common in travel writing and journalism.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {名所|めいしょ}{探訪|たんぼう}: visiting famous places\n- {現地|げんち}{探訪|たんぼう}: on-site investigation\n- {史跡|しせき}{探訪|たんぼう}: exploring historical sites\n- {探訪|たんぼう}{記|き}: travel report, exploration account\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {訪問|ほうもん}: visit — neutral, general-purpose visit without the exploratory nuance\n- {見学|けんがく}: tour, observation visit — educational or sightseeing focus\n- {取材|しゅざい}: news coverage — specifically journalistic investigation",
